From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:36:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 248/342] app_server: the font cache evicts no entry in use

The cache keeps 30 font entries and, making another, evicted the one
with the fewest uses per time since its last. An entry counts a use
only when recycled, so one being made and used had none and was always
the one. Drawing a string that needs fallbacks makes an entry for each
fallback family (eight with the colour emoji), so with the cache full
those entries evicted each other as they were made, the string's own
font's among them: its glyphs were made again at every draw, and the
fallback fonts opened again. 32 emoji at 12.5 points took 66 ms every
time (2 ms a picture, scaled again, and 12 ms of fonts), against 0.7 ms
from the cache at a size whose entries had been kept.

Entries in use (referenced beyond the cache's own reference) are left
out now; they live on anyway. With all of them in use, none is evicted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/app/font/FontCache.cpp | 26 +++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/servers/app/font/FontCache.cpp b/src/servers/app/font/FontCache.cpp
index f27e208f7b..1eff336155 100644
--- a/src/servers/app/font/FontCache.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/app/font/FontCache.cpp
@@ -124,26 +124,30 @@ FontCache::_ConstrainEntryCount()
 
 	FontMap::Iterator iterator = fFontCacheEntries.GetIterator();
 
-	// NOTE: if kMaxEntryCount has a sane value, there has got to be
-	// some entries, so using the iterator like that should be ok
-	FontCacheEntry* leastUsedEntry = iterator.Next().value;
+	// An entry in use (referenced by more than the map) is never the one:
+	// it lives on anyway, and the next use would make it again, without
+	// its glyphs. Entries are made in use and counted only when recycled,
+	// so a new one would always be the least used: drawing a string that
+	// needs fallbacks (each makes an entry) with the cache full evicted
+	// the entries it was making, its own font's among them, every time.
+	FontCacheEntry* leastUsedEntry = NULL;
+	double leastUsageIndex = 0;
 	bigtime_t now = system_time();
-	bigtime_t age = now - leastUsedEntry->LastUsed();
-	uint64 useCount = leastUsedEntry->UsedCount();
-	double leastUsageIndex = usage_index(useCount, age);
-//printf("  leastUsageIndex: %f\n", leastUsageIndex);
-
 	while (iterator.HasNext()) {
 		FontCacheEntry* entry = iterator.Next().value;
-		age = now - entry->LastUsed();
-		useCount = entry->UsedCount();
+		if (entry->CountReferences() > 1)
+			continue;
+		bigtime_t age = now - entry->LastUsed();
+		uint64 useCount = entry->UsedCount();
 		double usageIndex = usage_index(useCount, age);
 //printf("  usageIndex: %f\n", usageIndex);
-		if (usageIndex < leastUsageIndex) {
+		if (leastUsedEntry == NULL || usageIndex < leastUsageIndex) {
 			leastUsedEntry = entry;
 			leastUsageIndex = usageIndex;
 		}
 	}
+	if (leastUsedEntry == NULL)
+		return;
 
 	iterator = fFontCacheEntries.GetIterator();
 	while (iterator.HasNext()) {
